            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R1-001",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": ".github/workflows/ci.yml:524-526",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The CI job runs staticcheck via go run at a version tag, which fetches third-party code from the Go module proxy. The Go checksum database verifies the module and the job has only default checkout permissions. No exploit is reachable from this change, so this is a hardening note only.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  ".github/workflows/ci.yml:524-526"
                ],
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 23 manifest paths. The change adds a standard-library-only Go module, so it adds no third-party runtime dependency and no lockfile.",
              "Log files and meta files are opened read-only in telemetry/readers.go. The record struct decodes only usage, id, model and timestamp fields. Output holds aggregates only, and the tests in telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main_test.go assert that the sentinel content in the fixtures never reaches stdout.",
              "Log roots and the price file path come from local CLI flags. There is no network input, no shell execution, no privilege boundary and no secret handling, so I found no reachable injection, traversal or data exposure.",
              "Price parsing in telemetry/prices.go rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, trailing data, NaN, Infinity and negative rates. This limits unsafe input handling.",
              "The three review-receipt JSON files and the ledger and ADR documents are metadata only. They contain no secrets or credentials."
            ]
          }
        }
