              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "telemetry/readers.go:163-165",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "Pi dedupe uses a root-wide seen map populated only after a file is fully read, so rows with the same responseId inside different files are all kept if they are read before the first file's IDs are recorded. This is not a concern in practice because files are processed sequentially. The real residual gap is that a Pi line with neither responseId nor id is dropped and counted only as Skipped, with no distinct counter. This is low-impact and no test asserts it.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/readers.go:163-165",
                  "telemetry/readers_test.go:178-186"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-002",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go:108-121",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The 'By day' truncation depends on the positional boolean in the section table. TestTop covers --top 1 on days, but there is no test for a day count between 1 and the total with multiple retained days, so the 'latest N' ordering (relying on key sort order) is only proved for N=1.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go:108-121",
                  "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main_test.go:150-170"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 23 manifest paths. The change adds a new standalone module and one CI job, so there is no baseline behavior to regress.",
              "Failure paths are asserted with observable Stats and Call values in telemetry/readers_test.go: malformed lines, 2 MB lines, missing root, broken symlink, unreadable directory, mid-read I/O error that drops the file, bad or missing meta files, and per-file scoping of Pi fallback IDs.",
              "Determinism is covered by shuffled-insertion tests for recorded and estimated costs in telemetry/aggregate_test.go and by sorted emission in the readers.",
